(ned -- A PERPENDICULARITY, operator spec 2026-08-03.)
(MODEL. The rod slides DOWN PAST the puck at a standoff, then drives inward.)
(The puck does NOT need to extend downward: whatever station along the rod's)
(SHAFT is level with the puck makes contact, so every depth touches the SAME)
(feature with a DIFFERENT part of the rod. A vertical rod contacts at the)
(same Y at every depth; a rod tilted by A does not:)
(     recorded Y = constant - depth x tan A)
(The constant carries puck position, puck diameter, rod diameter and tip)
(centring, and it CANCELS in the difference. Both plunges are far below the)
(top, so the tip is clear of it and neither the tip's shape nor the puck)
(surface being out of perpendicular enters the measurement.)

(WHY DIVE DEEPER -- the resolution argument, and the math must honour it.)
(   tan of tilt = dY / dZ,  so  tilt = ATAN[dY]/[dZ])
(A touch repeats to about e, so the angle is uncertain by roughly e / dZ)
(radians. Every extra mm of dZ buys resolution LINEARLY and nothing else in)
(the expression depends on depth, which is the whole reason for -65:)
(   dZ = 40 mm  ->  5 um touch = 0.0072 deg)

(WHY BOTH PASSES USE THE SAME TWO DEPTHS. Measuring the AFTER pair at)
(different depths than the BEFORE pair buys nothing and costs accuracy: the)
(two passes would touch different stations along the rod and different points)
(on the puck, so rod straightness and local puck geometry stop cancelling and)
(start adding variance to the very comparison used to judge the correction.)
(Same depths, order REVERSED -- operator's original spec: touch top, touch)
(bottom, correct, touch bottom, touch top. Now dY and tilt are BOTH directly)
(comparable, and reversing the order means any drift with time or approach)
(direction shows up rather than hiding.)

(SEQUENCE, operator spec -- no travelling between touches, it is wasted time.)
(  BEFORE: probe at -25, back off, plunge to -65 AT THE BACKOFF STANDOFF,)
(          probe again.          dZ = 40 mm)
(  CORRECT A.)
(  AFTER:  probe at -65, back off, rise to -25, probe again. Same depths,)
(          reversed.             dZ = 40 mm)
(  Then lower the puck and park on the zero pose with the corrected A.)

(REQUIRES: rod stickout greater than the deep plunge -- 65 mm -- or the shaft)
(no longer spans the puck and nothing is touched.)

(Results: #3050 = dY before, #3051 = dY after, #3052 = A correction applied,)
(         #3053 = tilt before deg, #3054 = tilt after deg.)
(#3069 accumulates every A correction: it IS where A's true zero now sits on)
(the DRO, so cal_c_zero tilts about it and every routine parks there.)

o<cal_a_zero> sub
  #<cx>    = #1        (setter centre X, work frame -- from #3045)
  #<cy>    = #2        (setter centre Y, work frame -- from #3046)
  #<top>   = #3        (setter top Z, work frame -- from #3047)

  (MEASUREMENT FLOOR. Touches repeat to about 4 um, seen directly on)
  (2026-08-03: a BEFORE pair read 0.000 and the AFTER pair -0.004 over the)
  (same 40 mm. Below this, dY is noise and not tilt -- demanding an)
  (improvement there would reject a perfect result forever, which is exactly)
  (what happened. 0.010 mm over 40 mm is 0.014 deg.)
  #<tol> = 0.010

  #<d1> = 25.0         (before: shallow)
  #<d2> = 65.0         (before: deep)
  #<d3> = 65.0         (after: deep first)
  #<d4> = 25.0         (after: shallow)

  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, CAL A: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<top> EQ 0 AND #<cx> EQ 0 AND #<cy> EQ 0]
    (abort, CAL A: no setter centre - run StartPuck first)
  o6 endif

  (--- shared setup, GLOBAL so the file-level helper can read it -----------)
  #<_ca_cx>    = #<cx>
  #<_ca_cy>    = #<cy>
  #<_ca_top>   = #<top>
  (standoff mirrors cal_probe_center's r_out -- same clearance, same trip)
  #<_ca_stand> = 19.8
  (contact sits at radius 17.40, so 10 mm always trips first, and a)
  (no-contact fault stops 9.8 mm SHORT of centre instead of driving through)
  #<_ca_reach> = 10.0
  #<_ca_fpr>   = 100.0 (probe feed, operator spec)
  #<_ca_fla>   = 10.0  (latch feed, operator spec)
  #<_ca_ftr>   = 500.0 (traverse)
  #<_ca_fck>   = 200.0 (protective descent)
  (1 mm is plenty. A probe that will not release inside it is an ELECTRICAL)
  (contact fault -- fix the contact, not the distance. Operator 2026-08-03.)
  #<_ca_back>  = 1.0
  (clearance is 5 mm for every cal routine and IS the zero pose)
  #<_ca_safe>  = 5.0
  #<_ca_side>  = -1    (approach from -Y, probe toward +Y; +1 mirrors it)

  M50 P0               (pin the feed override -- probes run at programmed feed)
  M64 P3               (puck UP)
  G4 P1.5

  (=== BEFORE: -35, then -60 without leaving the standoff ==================)
  o<ca_touch> call [#<d1>] [1] [0]
  #<y1> = #<_ca_ty>
  o<ca_touch> call [#<d2>] [0] [0]
  #<y2> = #<_ca_ty>
  #<dy_b>   = [#<y2> - #<y1>]
  #<dz_b>   = [#<d2> - #<d1>]
  #<tilt_b> = [ATAN [#<dy_b>] / [#<dz_b>]]
  #3050 = #<dy_b>
  #3053 = #<tilt_b>
  (PRINT, CAL A BEFORE: y at -25 = #<y1>, y at -65 = #<y2>, DELTA Y = #<dy_b> over #<dz_b> mm, tilt #<tilt_b> deg)

  (=== ALREADY PERPENDICULAR? then there is nothing to correct ============)
  o115 if [ABS[#<dy_b>] LE #<tol>]
    #3051 = #<dy_b>
    #3054 = #<tilt_b>
    #3052 = 0
    G90
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
    M65 P3
    G4 P1.0
    G1 A#3069 C#3070 F600
    G1 X#<cx> Y#<cy> F[#<_ca_ftr>]
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
    M50 P1
    (PRINT, CAL A: dY #<dy_b> mm is within the #<tol> mm measurement floor - A is ALREADY perpendicular. Nothing applied, nothing to fix.)
    (DEBUG, CAL A ALREADY PERPENDICULAR: dY #<dy_b> mm, tilt #<tilt_b> deg - within the measurement floor)
    o115 return
  o115 endif

  (=== CORRECT ============================================================)
  #<corr> = [0 - #<tilt_b>]
  #3052 = #<corr>
  (PRINT, CAL A: rotating A by #<corr> deg)

  o120 if [ABS[#<corr>] GT 5.0]
    G90
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
    M65 P3
    M50 P1
    (abort, CAL A: computed correction over 5 deg - refusing to swing the head that far on one measurement)
  o120 endif

  (Rotating in place is what saves the climb. It is only safe while the swing)
  (at the deepest point stays inside the standoff clearance: at 65 mm depth)
  (0.5 deg moves the tip 0.57 mm against 2.40 mm of clearance. Bigger)
  (corrections climb out first, and the next touch then re-approaches.)
  #<next_app> = 0
  o125 if [ABS[#<corr>] GT 0.5]
    G90
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
    #<next_app> = 1
    (PRINT, CAL A: correction #<corr> deg exceeds 0.5 - climbing clear before rotating)
  o125 endif
  G91
  G1 A#<corr> F600
  G90
  #3069 = [#3069 + #<corr>]

  (=== AFTER: -65, then rise to -25, same standoff ========================)
  o<ca_touch> call [#<d3>] [#<next_app>] [0]
  #<y3> = #<_ca_ty>
  o<ca_touch> call [#<d4>] [0] [1]
  #<y4> = #<_ca_ty>
  (deeper minus shallower, so the sign convention matches the BEFORE pair)
  #<dy_a>   = [#<y3> - #<y4>]
  #<dz_a>   = [#<d3> - #<d4>]
  #<tilt_a> = [ATAN [#<dy_a>] / [#<dz_a>]]
  #3051 = #<dy_a>
  #3054 = #<tilt_a>
  (PRINT, CAL A AFTER: y at -65 = #<y3>, y at -25 = #<y4>, DELTA Y = #<dy_a> over #<dz_a> mm, tilt #<tilt_a> deg)

  (=== VERDICT, taken HERE while still at the standoff and clear of the puck)
  (Operator 2026-08-03: a correction that does not improve the ABSOLUTE)
  (distance is NOT applied. Both passes now share the same 40 mm baseline, so)
  (dY is directly comparable and is the test. A failed correction is ROLLED)
  (BACK -- leaving the head rotated by a move that made things worse would)
  (quietly corrupt the zero every later routine tilts about.)
  (Landing inside the measurement floor IS success, even if the number did)
  (not shrink -- at 4 um repeatability 0.006 -> 0.008 mm is the same reading)
  (twice, not a regression. Only a result that is BOTH outside the floor AND)
  (no better than before gets rolled back.)
  o130 if [ABS[#<dy_a>] LE #<tol> OR ABS[#<dy_a>] LT ABS[#<dy_b>]]
    (PRINT, CAL A OK: dY #<dy_b> -> #<dy_a> mm, tilt #<tilt_b> -> #<tilt_a> deg, A moved #<corr> deg. Kept.)
    (DEBUG, CAL A: dY #<dy_b> to #<dy_a> mm, A corrected #<corr> deg - KEPT)
  o130 else
    (roll the rotation back, here at the standoff where the puck is clear)
    G91
    G1 A[0 - #<corr>] F600
    G90
    #3069 = [#3069 - #<corr>]
    #3052 = 0
    (park and drop the puck BEFORE aborting -- an abort stops everything after)
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
    M65 P3
    G4 P1.0
    G1 A#3069 C#3070 F600
    G1 X#<cx> Y#<cy> F[#<_ca_ftr>]
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
    M50 P1
    (DEBUG, CAL A REVERTED: dY #<dy_b> to #<dy_a> mm - no improvement, A put back)
    (abort, CAL A: dY #<dy_b> then #<dy_a> mm - the correction did NOT improve the absolute distance, so it was ROLLED BACK and nothing was applied. A is where it started.)
  o130 endif

  (=== puck DOWN, park on the zero pose with the corrected A ==============)
  G90
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  M65 P3
  G4 P1.0
  G1 A#3069 C#3070 F600
  G1 X#<cx> Y#<cy> F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  M50 P1

o<cal_a_zero> endsub

M2 (end program)
